The attached image displays the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan adjuvant. Panel (A) is a transmission electron micrograph showing spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface, with a 50 nm scale bar. Panel (B) presents a histogram of the particle diameter, determined by dynamic light scattering, indicating a relatively narrow distribution predominantly between 30 and 110 nm, with a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter of 75-80 nm. These consistent physical characteristics are important for its role as an effective vaccine delivery vehicle that enhances antigen uptake by dendritic cells.